{
  "dataset_id": "offline-replay",
  "version": "offline-v1",
  "description": "\u00a714's offline dataset: every case is one checkable expectation about what a replayed run must achieve, grounded in the fixture ids `fixtures/scenarios.json` already names. It is authored as data rather than derived at load time so that a change to an expectation is a reviewable diff, and `dataset.py` validates every `scenario_id` and every reference id against that manifest at load.",
  "rubric": "offline-rules-v1",
  "synthetic": true,
  "partition_note": "`calibration` cases are the ones a rule was tuned against; `held_out` cases are the ones it was not. The split is per case rather than per scenario because a scenario usually contains both an obvious expectation and a sharp edge, and a split that separated whole scenarios would put every sharp edge on one side.",
